+# Chat SSE Keepalive
+
+*Implementation plan — 2026-08-06. GitHub issue #194. Run
+`01KZBR06NBP0QTDJRCFJR37P3M`.*
+
+## Status
+
+Ready for implementation. This is a narrowly scoped CLI/server transport
+repair. It adds comment traffic to the existing chat SSE response and focused
+server tests; it does not change chat events, replay semantics, browser state,
+or Bun's request timeout.
+
+## Outcome
+
+Every open `/api/projects/:project/chat/:skill/stream` response will write:
+
+```text
+: keepalive
+
+```
+
+every 15 seconds, including while the skill has no live chat session. Because
+the frame is an SSE comment, native `EventSource` consumes the bytes without
+dispatching a `message` event. The existing state snapshot, live events, and
+connect replay remain the only `data:` frames.
+
+The interval belongs to one response: it starts from that response's stream
+`start`, uses the same guarded enqueue path as chat data, and is cleared from
+the stream's `cancel`.
+
+## Verified current state
+
+The issue's central diagnosis matches the current code:
+
+- `packages/cli/src/server/Server.ts` defines `HEARTBEAT_MS = 15_000`,
+  starts one server-level interval, and broadcasts `: heartbeat\n\n` to
+  `/api/events-stream` subscribers.
+- The same server still configures `Bun.serve({ idleTimeout: 30 })`. Its
+  adjacent rationale treats 30 seconds as a safety net for ordinary cold-start
+  requests; this plan preserves both the value and rationale.
+- `packages/cli/src/server/ChatSessions.ts` builds the chat stream separately.
+  `streamResponse` currently sends `: connected\n\n`, one state `data:` frame,
+  buffered events when a live session exists, and later subscriber events. It
+  creates no heartbeat or keepalive interval.
+- `streamResponse` captures the live chat, if any, before constructing the
+  stream. With no live chat it deliberately leaves the response open after the
+  state snapshot, so the pre-session picker has the byte-idle case described by
+  the issue.
+- A live chat stores every broadcast event in `chat.events`; each new stream
+  replays that complete array. The viewer's `open` handler in
+  `packages/viewer/src/app/next/chatApi.ts` clears its event array because it
+  expects that replay. Neither behavior is part of this repair.
+- The viewer listens only for `message` events and parses their data. It has no
+  comment handler, and none is needed for a standards-compliant SSE comment.
+- The existing e2e stream collector in
+  `test/e2e/chat-sessions.e2e.test.ts` also reads only `data: ` lines. Its
+  connect replay, state, and event-order assertions therefore remain valid
+  without modification.
+- `ChatSessionManager` already has a separate manager-wide reap interval. Its
+  `stop()` clears that timer; connection keepalive timers must not be folded
+  into that unrelated lifecycle.
+- There is no existing proposal for issue #194.
+
+One report detail needs a routing-name refinement: after the machine-registry
+work, the browser-facing route is project-scoped
+(`/api/projects/:project/chat/:skill/stream`). `Server.ts` strips the project
+prefix and dispatches it to the same `ChatSessionManager.streamResponse`
+described in the issue. The transport defect and implementation location are
+otherwise unchanged.
+
+The repository alone establishes the missing-byte path and the 30-second
+timeout configuration. Browser reconnect timing and the reported scroll jump
+are field observations; this plan does not turn them into a second viewer
+change.
+
+## Design
+
+### One cadence value
+
+Move the current `HEARTBEAT_MS = 15_000` declaration from `Server.ts` to a
+small cycle-free server SSE module, then import it into both `Server.ts` and
+`ChatSessions.ts`. This preserves the machine stream's exact cadence while
+preventing a second independent 15,000 literal.
+
+Do not export the value from `Server.ts`: `Server` imports `ProjectRegistry`,
+which imports `ChatSessions`, so importing back from `Server` would create a
+runtime module cycle. Putting it in `ChatSessions.ts` would avoid that cycle
+but give a generic SSE transport setting a chat-specific owner, so the leaf
+module is the clearer shared boundary.
+
+### Per-response keepalive
+
+In `ChatSessionManager.streamResponse`:
+
+1. Retain an optional interval handle alongside the existing optional
+   subscriber.
+2. Define one guarded raw-frame writer in `start`. It catches enqueue failure
+   when a client disappears between interval ticks and stream cancellation.
+   Build `sendEvent` on that writer so comments and data have the same
+   disconnect behavior.
+3. Preserve the current order of `: connected`, state, and replayed events.
+   Start a `setInterval` from `start` that writes exactly
+   `: keepalive\n\n` every `HEARTBEAT_MS`.
+4. Schedule the interval independently of `chat`. Both live-session and
+   pre-session responses therefore get identical transport liveness.
+5. In `cancel`, clear this response's interval if assigned, then retain the
+   current subscriber removal.
+
+Add a short WHY comment citing issue #194: Bun's 30-second byte-idle safety
+net also applies to intentionally long-lived chat SSE responses, while an SSE
+comment keeps the socket active without creating a chat event.
+
+No keepalive enters `chat.events`, `chat.subscribers`, `ChatStreamEvent`, or
+`lastActivityAt`. In particular, transport activity must not prevent the
+existing idle-session reaper from ending a genuinely inactive agent session.
+
+## File-level implementation plan
+
+### 1. Share the existing heartbeat cadence
+
+Add `packages/cli/src/server/Sse.ts` with the single exported
+`HEARTBEAT_MS` constant and its issue-backed rationale.
+
+Update `packages/cli/src/server/Server.ts` to import that constant and remove
+only its local declaration. Leave `createEventBroadcaster`,
+`setInterval(broadcaster.onHeartbeat, HEARTBEAT_MS)`, server-stop cleanup, and
+`idleTimeout: 30` otherwise byte-for-byte unchanged.
+
+### 2. Keep chat responses alive
+
+Update `packages/cli/src/server/ChatSessions.ts` as described above. Keep the
+wire frame an unnamed SSE comment, not a `data:` frame; do not add a retry
+directive or a `ChatStreamEvent` member.
+
+Do not change the route handler in `Server.ts`, `ProjectRegistry`, the viewer,
+or replay-on-connect behavior.
+
+### 3. Add focused stream lifecycle tests
+
+Add `packages/cli/test/ChatSseKeepalive.test.ts`. Construct a real
+`ChatSessionManager` over a temporary root and minimal workspace config.
+Enable fake timers before construction because the constructor immediately
+starts the manager's existing reap interval. In unconditional cleanup, cancel
+every opened response reader, call `manager.stop()`, and only then restore real
+timers so neither connection intervals nor the reap interval can escape the
+test.
+
+Use Bun's fake timers against the production `HEARTBEAT_MS`; do not add an
+injectable production cadence merely to speed up tests. Cover:
+
+1. **Wire shape and cadence:** read the unchanged connected comment and initial
+   state frame, advance 15 seconds at a time, and assert each new chunk is
+   exactly `: keepalive\n\n`.
+2. **Long idle and pre-session:** open a stream for a skill with no live
+   session, advance 120 virtual seconds, observe eight keepalives, and verify
+   the reader remains open. This is the byte-idle case most likely to fail and
+   proves scheduling does not depend on `chat`.
+3. **No client-visible event:** collect `data:` payloads before and after the
+   virtual idle period and assert they are identical; every new frame must
+   start with `:`. The state snapshot therefore remains byte-identical and no
+   transcript event is introduced.
+4. **Per-connection cleanup:** record the fake-timer baseline from the
+   manager-wide reap timer, open N responses, and assert N additional timers.
+   Cancel every response reader and assert the count returns to baseline; then
+   `manager.stop()` returns it to zero. This proves both one timer per
+   connection and no accumulation after disconnect.
+
+Keep `test/e2e/chat-sessions.e2e.test.ts` unmodified and run it as the
+regression check for state/replay/event ordering. A real two-minute network
+test would make the normal suite materially slower and still duplicate the
+deterministic lifecycle test; perform the 120-second live-socket observation
+as acceptance validation instead.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run the narrow checks first, then the repository gates:
+
+```sh
+bun test packages/cli/test/ChatSseKeepalive.test.ts
+bun test test/e2e/chat-sessions.e2e.test.ts --timeout 30000
+bunx tsc --noEmit -p packages/core
+bunx tsc --noEmit -p packages/cli
+bun test packages
+bun test test/e2e --timeout 30000
+```
+
+No viewer source changes are planned, so a viewer-specific build is not
+required by this change. The unchanged full CI build may still be run as a
+final repository-wide gate.
+
+For live acceptance, open the pre-session chat stream in browser network tools
+or with an SSE-capable client, leave it inactive for at least 120 seconds, and
+verify:
+
+- one request remains open rather than a sequence of reconnects;
+- `: keepalive` arrives at approximately 15-second intervals;
+- the panel's transcript and state do not change; and
+- `/api/events-stream` continues its existing `: heartbeat` cadence.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- [ ] An idle chat SSE response remains open for at least 120 seconds in live
+      acceptance, with no server close or browser reconnect.
+- [ ] The chat stream emits exactly `: keepalive\n\n` at the shared
+      15,000-millisecond cadence.
+- [ ] A stream opened with no live session receives the same keepalives.
+- [ ] Keepalives add no `data:` payload, transcript item, state update,
+      buffered chat event, subscriber event, or session activity.
+- [ ] Canceling N chat streams clears all N connection intervals.
+- [ ] `/api/events-stream` still uses the same shared `HEARTBEAT_MS` and
+      `: heartbeat\n\n` frame.
+- [ ] `idleTimeout: 30` and its ordinary-request rationale remain unchanged.
+- [ ] Existing chat connect, replay, state, and event-order e2e tests pass
+      unmodified.
+- [ ] CLI typechecking and package/e2e test gates pass.
+
+## Risks and mitigations
+
+- **A disconnect races an interval tick.** Route comments and data through the
+  same try/catch-protected enqueue function, while `cancel` owns deterministic
+  timer cleanup.
+- **Fake timers include the manager's reap timer.** Assert relative to the
+  baseline, cancel every response, stop the manager, and restore real timers
+  in that order during unconditional test cleanup.
+- **A shared constant introduces an import cycle.** Keep it in the leaf
+  `Sse.ts` module imported by both consumers.
+- **Transport traffic accidentally counts as chat activity.** Write the raw
+  comment directly to the response only; never call `broadcast` or update
+  `lastActivityAt`.
+- **The test proves a stream abstraction but not browser networking.** Pair
+  deterministic 120-second virtual-time coverage with the explicit
+  120-second live acceptance observation; retain Bun's production
+  `idleTimeout: 30` so that observation exercises the original failure mode.
+
+## Deferred and out of scope
+
+- Issue #195's reconnect-safe transcript and scroll behavior.
+- Any change to connect replay, the viewer's `open` handler, or scroll policy.
+- Changing/removing `idleTimeout: 30` or adding per-route timeout exceptions.
+- A `retry:` directive or custom reconnect policy.
+- A keepalive data event, `ChatStreamEvent` schema change, or viewer handler.
+- Consolidating the machine and chat stream implementations beyond sharing
+  their cadence.
